Package: impliedIV
Type: Package
Title: Longitudinal Implied Interventions by Scaling an Instrument's Intensity
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Carlos", "García Meixide", email = "carlos.garcia@icmat.es",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates the mean outcome under stochastic interventions that
    multiply, by a factor alpha, the probability that a binary time-varying
    instrument (for example a prescription or a monitoring visit) fires at
    each visit, when the treatment it encourages (for example adherence) may
    be confounded with the outcome by unmeasured factors. The estimator is a
    longitudinal targeted maximum likelihood estimator (sequential regression)
    with monotone censoring; nuisance functions are estimated with Highly
    Adaptive Principal Components (package 'hapc') by default. Also reports
    the implied intervention on the treatment, and provides tools to build
    physician-preference instruments and to test the assumption that only the
    current instrument acts on the current treatment. Methodology:
    García Meixide and van der Laan, "Longitudinal implied interventions"
    (in preparation).
